SwiftPutty local patch 0020
Upstream: PuTTY 0.85 (a3cce3a48d4ab12e0fccb32998b9042d4f7c3ff1)
Status:   reported upstream (2026-10-19); suitable for upstream (undefined
          behaviour)

Terminal: a copied combining character takes its base cell's
attributes and colour.

add_cc() keeps combining characters in spare cells at the end of the
line and sets only their chr and cc_next. clipme() read attr and
truecolour from those cells for each combining character it copied,
so the clipboard's attribute and colour arrays (used by Windows' RTF
copy, and SwiftPutty's) held uninitialised values: undefined behaviour
for the truecolour flags (bools). Found by UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer on
Core/tests/fuzz/fuzz_terminal.c ("load of value 190, which is not a
valid value for type 'bool'"). Applies after patches 0004 and 0019.

--- a/terminal/terminal.c
+++ b/terminal/terminal.c
@@ -6705,10 +6705,17 @@
                 continue;
             }
 
+            /*
+             * A combining character takes the attributes and colour of
+             * the cell it combines with: add_cc() sets only the chr and
+             * cc_next of the spare cells it keeps them in, so their own
+             * attr and truecolour were never written.
+             */
+            attr = ldata->chars[x].attr;
+            tc = ldata->chars[x].truecolour;
+
             while (1) {
                 int uc = ldata->chars[x].chr;
-                attr = ldata->chars[x].attr;
-                tc = ldata->chars[x].truecolour;
 
                 switch (uc & CSET_MASK) {
